## Pipeline Responsibilities & Component Breakdown

### 1. `formula_engine/extractor.py` (Formula Extraction & Preprocessing)
- Scans Markdown for inline math (`$ ... $`) and display equations (`$$ ... $$`).
- Preprocesses and normalizes LaTeX syntax (normalizing whitespace, handling custom macros, protecting special mathematical symbols).

### 2. `formula_engine/converter.py` (External Converter Pipeline)
- Delegated LaTeX Parsing: Invokes `latex2mathml` to convert normalized LaTeX expressions into MathML XML.
- Delegated OMML Transformation: Transforms MathML into canonical Microsoft Office Math Markup Language (OMML) OpenXML nodes (`<m:oMath>` and `<m:oMathPara>`).
- Preserves native Cambria Math font styling across fractions, summations, integrals, radicals, matrices, piecewise cases, sub/superscripts, and Greek symbols.

### 3. `formula_engine/validator.py` (Validation & Build Gatekeeper)
- `validate_docx_xml(docx_path)`: Unzips the generated `.docx`, extracts `word/document.xml`, and performs a deep scan for forbidden raw LaTeX commands (`\frac`, `\sum`, `\lambda`, `\epsilon`, `\text{`, `\rightarrow`, `\alpha`, `\beta`, `\gamma`, `\Delta`, `\%`, `\_`, `\^`, `_{`, `^{`) and corrupted Unicode replacement characters (`U+FFFD`, `□`, `??`).
- **STRICT BUILD ABORT**: If ANY forbidden token or replacement character is detected inside `<w:t>` elements, the validator raises `ValidationError` and immediately halts export.
- `validate_omml_structure(docx_path)`: Verifies every equation is a valid `<m:oMath>` or `<m:oMathPara>` element.
- `validate_pdf(pdf_path)`: Inspects PDF binary/text for rendering parity.

### 4. `formula_engine/tests/test_formula_engine.py` (Automated Regression Test Suite)
- Test suite executing 100+ equations testing:
  - Simple & nested fractions
  - Summations, integrals, products, limits
  - Matrices (bmatrix, pmatrix, matrix)
  - Piecewise cases
  - Greek alphabet ($\alpha, \beta, \gamma, \delta, \epsilon, \lambda, \mu, \sigma, \Delta, \Sigma$)
  - Accents ($\bar{x}, \hat{x}, \vec{x}$)
  - Subscripts & superscripts
  - Inline math & display math
  - Equations inside table cells and figure captions
  - Equation right-aligned numbering tags `(1)`–`(5)`.

### 5. `formula_engine/publisher.py` (IEEE Document Generator)
- End-to-end publisher orchestrating document assembly for `paper2_academic_universe_growth_intelligence.md` into `Academic_Universe_Paper2_v1.0_IEEE_Final_OMML.docx` and `.pdf`.

